	'spec-sheets_h1' => 'Spec sheets',
	'spec-sheets_lede' => 'Every tile and stone reference in our library is documented on a dedicated specification sheet. Amira Haddad issues completed sheets within 48 hours for architects, builders, and homeowners.',
	'spec-sheets_s1_b' => 'A specification sheet records eight essential technical fields: range and code, format and thickness, surface finish, slip rating, edge type, shade variation, joint width with grout colour, and stock lead time. Format indicates exact production dimensions in centimetres and millimetres, whether standard 60 × 120 cm porcelain slabs or 6.5 × 20 cm glazed wall tiles. Surface finishes distinguish between matt, honed, brushed, split face, and soft-polish textures. Slip ratings clearly define barefoot and shod wet traction in plain, verifiable terms so specifiers can confidently allocate materials to wet areas, stairs, or living floors.',
	'spec-sheets_s1_h' => 'Formats, finishes, and slip ratings',
	'spec-sheets_s2_b' => 'Edge descriptions identify whether a tile has sharp, mechanically rectified edges for narrow 2 mm joints or a traditional cushion edge for softer transitions. Shade variation is classified using the standard V1 to V4 rating scale. V1 indicates uniform appearance with minimal tone drift, while V2 denotes slight variation across batches. Natural stone like limestone and slate generally carries V3 moderate or V4 substantial variation, where every quarried slab presents distinct veining and tonal depth. Understanding these ratings beforehand ensures your contractor installs material with balanced, deliberate composition.',
	'spec-sheets_s2_h' => 'Rectified edges and shade variation codes',
	'spec-sheets_s3_b' => 'Our spec sheets specify required joint widths alongside recommended tones from our 24 grout colours. We also record real-time factory availability and lead times, giving you accurate dispatch windows for kerbside pallet delivery. Amira Haddad manages architectural enquiries and emails PDF specification sheets within 48 hours of your request. To request documentation for any porcelain, stone, glazed tile, or terrazzo sample, email hello@yuka-tiles.example or speak with our team during a window appointment at Saltgate Works.',
	'spec-sheets_s3_h' => 'Joints, lead times, and sheet requests',
	'spec_h' => 'What a spec sheet records',
	'spec_label' => 'Specification sheet',
	'spec_more' => 'All spec sheets →',
	'spec_note' => 'Amira Haddad checks every field against the range before a sheet leaves the showroom. Architects, builders and homeowners get the full sheet within 48 hours of asking.',
	'stat1' => 'ranges on the window wall',
	'stat2' => 'samples to borrow',
	'stat3' => 'days per loan',
	'stat4' => 'to send a spec sheet',
	'terms_h1' => 'Loan terms',
	'terms_lede' => 'Our loan terms are designed to make testing tile and stone in your own daylight straightforward and reliable. Here is how our loan service operates.',
	'terms_s1_b' => 'You may borrow up to five standard 30 × 30 cm cut samples from our five material ranges on a single loan card. Standard samples are completely free to borrow for seven days. This week-long duration allows you to assess each surface under natural morning, midday, and evening daylight, and compare it against your joinery, paint, and fabrics. If your project schedule or client review requires additional evaluation time, you may extend your loan once by seven days by notifying us at hello@yuka-tiles.example prior to your original return date.',
	'terms_s1_h' => 'Sample allowances and seven-day duration',
	'terms_s2_b' => 'Large-format 60 × 120 cm display boards carry a refundable EUR 40 deposit per board, payable at collection. When you return the boards to our counter at Saltgate Works in sound, undamaged condition, your EUR 40 deposit is refunded in full to your payment method. Samples that are lost, broken, or not returned after an approved loan period will be charged at the standard replacement sample cost noted on each range\'s specification sheet. Returned samples are checked, cleaned, and re-shelved by Tomasz Wieczorek each afternoon.',
	'terms_s2_h' => 'Large-format boards and return conditions',
	'thanks_h1' => 'Thanks',
	'thanks_lede' => 'Thank you for contacting Yuka Tiles at Saltgate Works. We have received your request and look forward to assisting with your project.',
	'thanks_s1_b' => 'A member of our team will review your message and reply within one working day. If you requested sample loans, Tomasz Wieczorek will confirm that your selected tiles are packed and ready for collection at our Eastmere counter. For architectural specification enquiries, Amira Haddad will compile and email your technical spec sheets within 48 hours. If you booked a window appointment, we will confirm your requested 60-minute session at 10:00, 11:30, or 13:00.',
	'thanks_s1_h' => 'What happens next with your enquiry',
	'thanks_s2_b' => 'Our showroom at Saltgate Works, Unit 3, 21 Weaver Street, Eastmere is open Tuesday to Saturday from 10:00 to 18:00, with Thursday evening hours until 20:00. If you wish to view our window wall before receiving our reply, feel free to stop by during opening hours. You can examine porcelain, natural stone, glazed tile, terrazzo, and our 24 grout colours in direct sunlight at the low oak bench.',
	'thanks_s2_h' => 'Visiting us while you wait',
